# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values:
#   cp .env.sample .env
#
# Optional — if unset, the script generates a fresh wallet on each run and
# prints the private key. Re-runs must reuse the same key to redeem from the
# same balances.
#
# Both scenarios sign from the SAME native Push EOA. Gas is paid in PC. No
# Sepolia ETH is needed for either flow.
#
# Fund this Push EOA with:
#   • PC for gas — https://faucet.push.org/
#       Scenario 1 needs only enough for the redeem tx (a fraction of a PC).
#       Scenario 2 needs ≥ 5 PC (gas + outbound swap to Sepolia).
#   • PUSD ≥ 1 on this EOA. Easiest source:
#       Run ../pusd-mint-from-push-eoa with this same key first — it mints
#       PUSD into the EOA. (PUSD minted via ../pusd-mint-from-external-chain
#       lands on the UEA, not on this EOA — different address on Push.)
PUSH_PRIVATE_KEY=
